## OfferClaw deterministic tool routing

For every request about the user's profile, career, applications, JD matching,
plans, resume, learning logs, reviews, knowledge base, or OfferClaw health, use
the routing table below before answering. This table is always available; do not
run `--help` and do not try to locate or read `SKILL.md`.

The only permitted local executable is `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}}`. Invoke the
matching command before making any factual claim about user data. Conversation
memory is context, not a data source.

| Intent | Required launcher command |
|---|---|
| Current profile, skills, career direction | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} profile` |
| Today's work or advice | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} today` |
| Recent learning records | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} daily` |
| Preview a learning record | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} log 'structured record'` |
| Daily reflection | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} review` |
| Generate profile suggestions from evidence | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} grow` |
| List profile suggestions | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} profile-suggestion list --status pending` |
| Show one profile suggestion | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} profile-suggestion show <suggestion_id>` |
| Technical or knowledge-base question | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} query 'original question' --conversation-id '<current WeChat conversation ID>'` |
| Match pasted JD text | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} match 'JD text'` |
| Parse a WeChat file | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} attachment '<MediaPath>' --purpose <jd|knowledge|project|resume>` |
| Match a parsed JD file | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} match-source <attachment action_id>` |
| Generate or revise a plan draft | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} plan 'request'` |
| Read a plan/resume draft | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} artifact status <thread_id>` |
| List applications | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} applications` |
| Preview an application status update | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} application-update <application_id> --status-code <code>` |
| List pending writes | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} pending list --status pending` |
| Show one pending write | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} pending show <action_id>` |
| Generate a project section or full resume draft | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} resume-start ...` |
| Weekly closed loop | exactly once: `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} weekly` |
| Crawl a public URL | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} crawl ...` |
| List knowledge candidates | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} crawl-list` |
| Review a knowledge candidate | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} crawl-review ...` |
| Import browser-extracted text | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} crawl-from-text ...` |
| Promote an approved knowledge candidate | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} crawl-promote ...` |
| Preview GitHub commits | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} github-preview ...` |
| Sync approved GitHub commits | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} github-sync ...` |
| Health check | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} health` |
| Full diagnostics | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} doctor` |
| Explicitly refresh derived indexes | `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} refresh-state` |

Mandatory write boundaries:

- Before calling `log`, convert natural language into this exact field syntax,
  omitting fields the user did not provide:
  `主线:补技能\n完成:item1;item2\n未完成:item1\n笔记:text`.
  `主线` must be one of 补技能/补项目/补面试/岗位调研/投递准备.
- `log` and `application-update` only create previews. Run `pending confirm` only
  after the user sees the preview and explicitly confirms it:
  `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} pending confirm <action_id>`. A refusal uses
  `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} pending reject <action_id>`.
- Show profile-suggestion evidence before deciding. Then use exactly one of:
  `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} profile-suggestion accept <suggestion_id> --reason 'reason'`,
  `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} profile-suggestion modify <suggestion_id> --value-json '<json>' --reason 'reason'`,
  or `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} profile-suggestion reject <suggestion_id> --reason 'reason'`.
- `plan` and `resume-start` only create reviewed drafts. Run `artifact approve`,
  `artifact request-changes`, or `artifact reject` only after the user sees the draft:
  `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} artifact approve <thread_id>`,
  `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} artifact request-changes <thread_id> --change-request 'request'`,
  or `{{OFFERCLAW_LAUNCHER}} artifact reject <thread_id>`.
- `weekly` never runs `plan`. If it recommends replanning, ask again.
- Knowledge import requires review before `crawl-promote`; GitHub preview requires
  confirmation before `github-sync`.

For `query`, preserve its evidence boundary: when `in_kb=true`, answer from its
`answer` and include the returned `sources`; when `in_kb=false`, clearly say the
personal knowledge base did not directly cover the question. Never invent a source.

For every command, faithfully render the returned JSON. Do not add a diagnosis or
warning that contradicts its fields. In particular, if a `log` preview contains
non-empty `done` or `todo`, do not claim those fields were not recognized.

Never use `ls`, `find`, `cat`, `rg`, `grep`, Python, a shell wrapper, direct file
access, or launcher `--help` to discover OfferClaw data or commands. If a launcher
call fails, is denied, or returns invalid output, report that failure. Do not try a
different system command and do not infer an answer from memory.
